# Oddlot — Cursor rules

These rules replace the PRD's `AGENTS.md`.

**Canonical specs for agents:**
- Full master PRD: `docs/master-prd.md`
- UBC hackathon guide: `docs/hackathon-guide-ubc-2026.md`
- Root `PRD.md` is only an index into those docs

Spec sections in `docs/master-prd.md` (Program through Web app, Acceptance tests, Milestones) win over narrative. If two spec sections conflict, stop and ask.

## Decide, log, continue

When something is unspecified, pick the simplest option consistent with `docs/master-prd.md`. Record it in `DECISIONS.md` (date, decision, reason, workstream) and keep going.

## Scope

Build P0, then P1, in MVP order. Add nothing else: no extra tickers, features, chains, or mainnet.

Cut order if behind: P2 → P1 charts → Gemini hedge. Never cut collateral checks, auto-exercise, or the Protect screen.

## Tests define done

Write each milestone's acceptance tests first. A milestone is done only when they pass in CI or a recorded local run.

## Frozen interfaces

After M0, these are frozen: `config/oddlot.json`, program accounts/instructions/events, and `schemas/api/*`. To change one, update the spec, every consumer, and `DECISIONS.md` in the same change.

## Check live docs

Use the latest stable Anchor, Pyth, QuickNode, and Gemini APIs. Read current docs before coding against them; do not rely on memory.

## Never

- Commit keypairs, API keys, or `.env` files
- Touch mainnet or real funds
- Use floating-point math on-chain
- Weaken a program check to make a test pass

## Stop and ask a human when

- You need an account, API key, captcha, or faucet
- A frozen interface must change
- An acceptance test cannot pass as written
- Anything would cost real money

## Keep it runnable

At every milestone, `README.md` has working commands to build, test, and run each part locally.

## Workstreams

| WS | Path | Stack |
|----|------|--------|
| WS1 Program | `programs/oddlot`, `tests/` | Rust + Anchor, Token-2022, Pyth |
| WS2 Pricer | `pricer/` | Python 3.12, FastAPI |
| WS3 Keeper | `keeper/` | TypeScript, Node |
| WS4 Web app | `app/` | Next.js App Router, Tailwind, wallet adapter |

Single-agent order: WS1 → WS2 → WS3 → WS4. Parallel after M0 freezes shared contracts.
